      {
        "id": 236292,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-03-23T15:49:27.202Z",
        "cooked": "<p>A lot of fun hearing Paul again. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"> Here’s to that supposed Editor’s Note happening! I’m sorry we don’t get to see the pirate coat.</p>\n<p>Daniel Spaniel’s letter got me thinking about the Humanverse, where most of the characters are the same except all the non-human ones are human, and “Human” is both a legitimate first and last name. So you’ve got the Human Tempest, the Human Sky-Scraper (which are very reasonable hero names, I think you will agree), Human Warlord Voss, Humantron-X, and that tortured would-be villain from the Enclave of the Humans, Deadhuman, later known as Lifehuman. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/drooling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":drooling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":drooling_face:\"></p>\n<p>Okay, but a one-off comment by Christopher begs a question I’ve been pondering lately: Is Nightmist named after Adam’s sister, as Argent Adept was named after Christopher’s brother?</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-03-23T15:49:27.202Z",
