        "raw": "A lot of fun hearing Paul again. :) Here's to that supposed Editor's Note happening! I'm sorry we don't get to see the pirate coat.\n\nDaniel Spaniel's letter got me thinking about the Humanverse, where most of the characters are the same except all the non-human ones are human, and \"Human\" is both a legitimate first and last name. So you've got the Human Tempest, the Human Sky-Scraper (which are very reasonable hero names, I think you will agree), Human Warlord Voss, Humantron-X, and that tortured would-be villain from the Enclave of the Humans, Deadhuman, later known as Lifehuman. :drooling_face:\n\nOkay, but a one-off comment by Christopher begs a question I've been pondering lately: Is Nightmist named after Adam's sister, as Argent Adept was named after Christopher's brother?",
