        "raw": "[quote=\"TakeWalker, post:2, topic:28316\"]\nOkay, but a one-off comment by Christopher begs a question I’ve been pondering lately: Is Nightmist named after Adam’s sister, as Argent Adept was named after Christopher’s brother?\n[/quote]\n\nFrom the first live Gen Con episode:\n\nWho's named for real people? Anthony Drake for Christopher's brother. [Paul Parsons](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Legacy) for Adam's brother. [Aldred Industries](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Omnitron) is tied to Paul Bender's family and [Maia Montgomery](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Wraith) for his wife. [Pete Riske](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Setback), [Eaken-Rubendaal Laboratories](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Eaken-Rubendaal_Laboratories), [President Hargett](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=President_Hargett&action=edit&redlink=1), [Grand Warlord Voss](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Grand_Warlord_Voss), and [Tyler Vance](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Bunker) are named for friends. [Vanessa Long](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Visionary) is named for Adam's wife. In general, there's no connection between the real person and the in-game person or entity (Anthony's *music* and Pete being exceptions). There are more examples that are being withheld for privacy reasons.\n\nEdit - Shoot, I got interrupted as I was going through the process of looking this up and copy/pasting it and so forgot to actually check if Faye was even mentioned. *facepalm*",
